## Root cause

`AwaitFinder` (`crates/oxc_linter/src/rules/eslint/require_await.rs:220-239`) only sets `found` for `await` expressions and `for await`. An `await using` declaration also awaits (the resource's disposal when the scope exits), so an async function whose only await is `await using x = ...` or `for (await using x of xs)` is reported.

The rule's dangerous fix then removes `async`, which leaves `await using` outside an async function. With oxlint 1.85.0:

```js
// input
export async function f() {
  await using x = getResource();
}

// after --fix-dangerously
export function f() {
  await using x = getResource();
}
```

The fixed file no longer parses (`` `await` is only allowed within async functions and at the top levels of modules ``). In a debug build the same fix trips the fixer's syntax check (`crates/oxc_linter/src/fixer/mod.rs:422`).

ESLint counts these declarations since eslint/eslint#19828 ([`lib/rules/require-await.js#L180-L182`](lib/rules/require-await.js#L180-L182)):

```js
if (node.kind === "await using") {
	scopeInfo.hasAwait = true;
}
```

## Fix

Override `visit_variable_declaration` in `AwaitFinder`: an `await using` declaration sets `found`, any other declaration is walked as before. This mirrors the existing `visit_for_of_statement` override. The left side of `for (await using x of xs)` reaches the same method through `walk_for_of_statement` -> `visit_for_statement_left`, so it needs no separate case. Nested functions and arrows are still not v
